@* Checkbox's Overview, written by hand after Button's, Card's and MultiSelect's: what it posts,
   a box that must be checked, the indeterminate state (select all on interactive pages), the
   row's layout (shown on Switch's page) and states.
   Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A checkbox is a box with a label that the user checks for one yes-or-no choice. It suits a single choice, such as agreeing to the terms.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>For a setting that reads as on or off, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/switch">Switch</Anchor>. For several choices from a list, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/checkbox-group">CheckboxGroup</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">What it posts</Heading>
<TextBlock>A checked box posts <Code>true</Code>. An unchecked box posts <Code>false</Code> from a hidden field that follows it, so a property that defaults to true can be turned off on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor>. A disabled box posts nothing.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Agreeing to terms</Heading>
<TextBlock>A terms box must be checked before the form can be saved, and its label often has a link. For a label with markup, such as a link, write it as the checkbox's <Code>ChildContent</Code>. To require the box to be checked, add <Code>[Required]</Code> and <Code>[Range(typeof(bool), "true", "true")]</Code> to the property.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-terms" />
<List>
    <ListItem><Code>[Required]</Code> makes the browser stop the form post until the box is checked.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>A bool is never null, so <Code>[Required]</Code> always passes on the server. <Code>[Range]</Code> is the check there.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Give both the same <Code>ErrorMessage</Code>. With IzzyBlazor's script, the browser shows it too.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Indeterminate state</Heading>
<TextBlock>The indeterminate state is a dash in the box. It shows that only some of what the box stands for is checked, as on a box that selects a list of others. Set <Code>Indeterminate</Code> to show it, and on interactive pages set the other boxes from the box's <Code>ValueChanged</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-select-all" />
<TextBlock>Nothing links the boxes but your C#, so this works on interactive pages only. For a select-all box that works on static pages too, use a CheckboxGroup with <Code>SelectAll</Code>; see <Anchor Href="docs/components/checkbox-group#select-all">Select all</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Hints, icons and the end of the row</Heading>
<TextBlock>To add help under the label, set <Code>Hint</Code>. To show an icon at the row's start, set <Code>Icon</Code>, and to put the box at the end of the row, as on a Switch, set <Code>ControlPosition.End</Code>. The Switch page shows them in <Anchor Href="docs/components/switch#at-the-end-of-the-row">At the end of the row</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>The size lines a checkbox up with buttons and other fields. Set <Code>Size</Code> to choose one. For a box that can't change, set <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-sizes" />
<TextBlock>There's no <Code>ReadOnly</Code>, because HTML has no read-only checkbox: in a read-only <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>, the box is disabled while a hidden field posts its value. A disabled box posts nothing. Before saving a disabled value from a form post, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* The label comes from the property's [Display(Name)], or Label. *@
        <Checkbox @bind-Value="Model!.Subscribe" />
        <Checkbox @bind-Value="Model!.RememberMe" Label="Keep me signed in" />

        @* A label with markup. *@
        <Checkbox @bind-Value="Model!.AcceptTerms">
            I agree to the <Anchor Href="terms">terms of service</Anchor>
        </Checkbox>
        """;
}
